              "summary": "**Evaluating CVSS for CORS Attacks**\n\nI\u2019m noticing that many CVSS evaluations categorize the attack vector as AV L for loopback CORS cross-browser attacks. This choice seems to arise because the attacker is positioned externally. I find it interesting how these classifications can shape our understanding of vulnerabilities. It's important to think about how different attack scenarios might affect this assessment. I want to ensure that I\u2019m clearly conveying the reasoning and implications behind such evaluations.",
